edit(8,[('High force per compact actuator, but pumps/plumbing and seal leakage/friction must be included in full-system assessment.','This preserves the actuator versus system boundary.'),('High actuator power-to-weight implies the same whole-system advantage even when the pump and reservoir are excluded from the mass estimate.','Excluding peripheral mass cannot establish the complete-system ratio.'),('Direct joint drive means seal friction can be omitted when evaluating precise force control.','Removing a gearbox does not remove cylinder seal friction.'),('Fluid leakage affects only appearance and cannot change maintenance or usable actuator performance.','The source identifies leakage as a meaningful drawback, not merely cosmetic.')])
