edit(49,[('Measured q belongs to observation/state information; issued PWM is an action; the +10 success score comes from the reward rule.','Measurement, command and scoring rule play distinct roles.'),('The requested target angle is the measured encoder observation; measured q is the action; +10 is the reward.','A desired target is not the measured angle, and the measurement is not the issued command.'),('Measured q is observation information; the stable-grasp success score is the motor action; PWM is the reward.','This interchanges the physical command and the designer’s success score.'),('Measured q and the PWM command are both measured physical state; +10 is the observed contact force.','An issued command is not thereby a measurement, and the numeric score is not a force reading.')],stem='An encoder reports q, a policy issues a PWM command, and a designed rule awards +10 when the measured grasp satisfies its success condition. Which assignment matches the source’s observation/action/reward roles?',typ='scenario',why='The encoder supplies measured position information, the PWM command implements the selected action, and the designer maps success evidence to a numeric reward. These roles do not establish that q alone is a complete Markov state.');premise(49)
