edit(53,[('+10 is a designed score for satisfying both conditions; the force reading is evidence for only the force condition.','The supplied conjunction requires both acceptable force and target placement.'),('A stable 6 N grasp earns +10 even if the object is outside the target region.','That ignores the stated placement condition.'),('Any force of at least 7 N earns +10 because a stronger grasp necessarily satisfies the stated band.','Values above the upper bound do not satisfy the declared 5–7 N interval.'),('A stable 6 N grasp inside the target region earns +6 because the score must equal the numeric force.','The reward rule explicitly assigns +10 rather than copying the force value.')],stem='In an added reward design, award +10 only when grasp force stays within 5–7 N and the object is inside the target region; otherwise award 0. Which interpretation is correct?',typ='scenario',why='Reward is a specified mapping of measured task conditions to a score. Here both force-band and placement tests must pass; the reward number is not a physical force unit.',assumptions=['Added conjunctive reward rule with an inclusive 5–7 N force band; stability is evaluated over the declared task interval.']);premise(53)
