edit(66,[('Bias 0.4 m; variance 0.02 m².','The shared fixed bias survives averaging, while the independent noise variances combine with squared one-half weights.'),('Bias 0 m; variance 0.02 m².','Noise averaging does not remove the shared fixed offset.'),('Bias 0.4 m; variance 0.04 m².','This retains the single-sensor noise variance rather than the independent average’s variance.'),('Bias 0.2 m; variance 0.02 m².','Both inputs contain the same 0.4 m bias; averaging them does not halve that common component.')],stem='In an added scalar model, each of two position sensors has error e_i=b+η_i. The shared fixed bias is b=0.4 m; η1 and η2 are independent zero-mean noises, each with variance 0.04 m². For the equal average, use Var((η1+η2)/2)=(v1+v2)/4. What are its bias and error variance?',typ='numerical',difficulty='medium',why='Averaging independent noise can reduce variance without removing a common fixed bias. The combined estimate is still biased by 0.4 m even though its random error variance falls to 0.02 m².',steps=['Average error=(b+η1+b+η2)/2=b+(η1+η2)/2.','Its expectation is b=0.4 m.','Its variance is (0.04+0.04)/4=0.02 m²; the fixed bias is not a random variance contribution.'],forms=[formula('e_avg = b+(η1+η2)/2; E[e_avg]=b; Var(e_avg)=(v1+v2)/4',{'e_avg':'error of the equal-weight average estimate','b':'shared fixed error offset','η1,η2':'independent zero-mean random errors','v1,v2':'variances of η1 and η2','E':'expectation operator','Var':'variance operator'},{'e_avg,b,η1,η2':'m','v1,v2,Var(e_avg)':'m²'},['Added independent zero-mean noise model; b is fixed, not a random common error; variance is not mean squared error.'])],assumptions=['Added explicit scalar error model; no Gaussian assumption is required for this mean/variance result.']);premise(66)
